Port osu!stable's spinner requirements and grading to opsu!.

Upstream opsu! used a hand-measured approximation carrying its own
"TODO not correct at all, but close enough?" and "TODO: verify ratios"
comments:

	float spinsPerMinute = 100 + (overallDifficulty * 15);

That is roughly 2.9 rotations per second at OD 5 and 4.2 at OD 10.
osu!stable requires a sustained 3 rot/s at OD 0, 5 rot/s at OD 5 and
7.5 rot/s at OD 10, so opsu! spinners cleared far too easily -- often
with bonus score to spare on maps where stable would award a 100.

Grading is also absolute in stable rather than ratio based: a full
clear is a 300, one rotation short is a 100 and two short is a 50.
The on-screen spinner meter still uses rotations / rotationsNeeded and
is unaffected.

